-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Owner       Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-03

  Replay      lockstep memory, registers and picture IDENTICAL on 8 scripted
              recordings, 20982 game frames, default and Enhanced (both
              without outline or paper edge, seams closed); negatives
              detected: 7 (engine), 4 for the default figure edges (the old
              default, outline kept, paper edge kept, seams open), 15 for
              Enhanced (player, player 2, rotation map, pick-up keys, store
              off, outline kept, paper edge kept, the third pass, paper border
              painted, skin outside an enemy face, enemy without a face, seams
              open, the fourth pass, the fifth pass, the 17:00 build)

  Emulator    JNext headless, plain, sprites and Enhanced reach play from the
              file's start; default and Enhanced through the Browser and the
              loader, output byte-exact with apply

  Coverage    level 1 to beyond the bridge, one and two players, wading, game
              over, attract; no level end; no tank seen driven

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
